 ## Overview
-Mesh Voxelization converts a continuous polygon mesh (typically STL or OBJ) into a discrete 3D grid of voxels, determining the occupancy (solid/empty) and optionally the signed distance field (SDF) for each cell [S1, S4, unofficial]. It solves the problem of discretizing surface geometry for volume rendering, simulation, or 3D printing preparation [G]. Unlike [Mesh to Voxel Generation via AABB-Triangle Intersection](3775-mesh-to-voxel-generation-vvia-aabb-triangle-intersection.md), which relies on bounding box overlap, or [Template-based Voxelization](7964-template-based-voxelization.md), which uses precomputed patterns, this method uses ray casting to robustly determine topological inside/outside status, handling complex concavities and open meshes via multi-directional sampling [S2, S4, unofficial].
